[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1880","stub":{"id":"1880","section":"02. Sinawava to South Campground (Zion NP)","altname":"","river":"Virgin, N. Fork","difficulty":"IIItoV","states":["USA-UTA"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"50","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:50:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112654","location":{"latitude":"37.285","longitude":"-112.948"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"117941","location":{"latitude":"37.202","longitude":"-112.987"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"8.5","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"101247990","title":null,"post_date":"2011-04-25 04:00:00+00","detail":"Lots of sweepers in first five miles could cause problems for inexperienced boaters. Floods this winter uprooted and bent many trees. Lower water will force boaters into cutbanks with trees extending into main channel. Higher water, above 1200-ish cfs, could float new debris and create new hazards.","user":{"name":" "}},{"id":"101247899","title":null,"post_date":"2011-04-15 04:00:00+00","detail":"River-wide strainer at Birch Creek Bridge/Court of the Patriarchs. Also, the word is that some new rocks washed into the run and/or existing rocks moved during the December flood.","user":{"name":"Rob Gauss"}}],"photos":[{"id":"13770","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9275","description":"gets a bit pushy at this level","caption":"Bottom Corral Falls","poi_name":"Corral Falls","subject":"Adrian Clarke","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13770","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13770"}},{"id":"42835","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"2843","description":"Looking upstream from the bridge on the Emerald Pool trail, shows the placid nature of the river along much of this section.","caption":"Zion near Emerald Pool trail","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/42835","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/42835"}},{"id":"42836","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"2843","description":"Looking downstream at the NF Virgin from the trail to Emerald Pools.  The trail foot bridge is in the center of the picture.","caption":"Zion scene 2","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/42836","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/42836"}},{"id":"42837","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"2843","description":"A low water view from the road somewhere along the Satan's Staircase section.   The creek gets steep and congested in this section.  ","caption":"Virgin River boulders","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/42837","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/42837"}},{"id":"42834","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"2843","description":"Just upstream from the end of the road at the Temple of Sinawava.","caption":"Zion scene 1","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Paul Martzen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/42834","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/42834"}},{"id":"13772","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9275","description":"","caption":"High Water","poi_name":"Satans Staircase","subject":"John Blake","author":"Ute ?","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13772","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13772"}}],"detail":{"id":"1880","permitUrl":"http://www.nps.gov/zion/planyourvisit/rivertrips.htm","permitInfo":"Boating allowed when flows exceed 140 cfs","description":"SEASON: From mid April to the end of May. The river typically peaks around the beginning of May.\n\nFUN FACT: The best way to experience Zion National Park\n\nPERMIT: Entrance fee to the park and a free backcountry permit are required to float this reach through [Zion National Park](http://www.nps.gov/zion). It's a good idea to double check the park's river-running policy before heading out.\n\nLOGISTICS: A shuttle road parrallels the run and park users are required to use the bus system which provides a convenient shuttle. From the last bus stop it's an easy walk on a paved trail to the put-in.\n\nDESCRIPTION:\n\nThe North Fork of the Virgin is a fun river that provides the best means of experiencing one of our country's most beautiful national parks. There's some good whitewater on this run along with absolutely stunning geology.\n\nFrom the put-in at the Temple of Sinawava the river starts out as mostly class II for the first 5 miles, although it can push class III at higher flows. Stay alert for wood hazards. Those who are looking for the easier trip can take out above the Birch Creek Bridge at the Court of the Patriarchs parking area. Those looking for more action can continue through Satan's Staircase which starts just downstream of the Birch Creek Bridge.\n\nThe action through Satan's Staircase kicks off with Corral Falls and then you encounter over a mile of fun boulder garden rapids which push class V at higher water  but drop down to III/IV at the lower limit of flows.\n\n2012: At higher flows it may not be possible to get under the riverwide wood right after Corral Falls. Watch out for other sweepers a mile below there.\n\nThe action tapers off a bit at Flannigan Diversion and calms down to class III, but the run continues for another mile and half to the bridge at the visitor center near South and Watchman campgrounds. There is some potential boating below this point but you need to be aware of private property when selecting your access point.\n\nfor additional information see:\n\n[Virgin River Runners Coalition web site](http://www.virginriver.org) which includes detailed descriptions of the different sections\n\nNichols, G.C. 2002. River Runners' Guide to Utah. University of Utah Press, includes an excellent and comprehensive description\n\nNational Geographic's Trails Illustrated Map 214 of Zion National Park is a good map of the river\n\n[Zion National Park](http://www.nps.gov/zion)","averageGradient":"55","maxGradient":"110","length":"8.2","correlations":[{"reachID":"1880","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"150","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"600"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"NORTH FORK VIRGIN RIVER NEAR SPRINGDALE, UT","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"09405500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"50","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:50:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"7.33","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:50:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"37.2097046","longitude":"-112.9785512"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/09405500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/09405500/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":"Previous Flowbands: \nRange of Boatable Flows (R0-R9): 150 - 600 cfs  Comment: Boating is allowed above 140 cfs; but over 250 is better.\n\nMigration Errors: \nSingle range is valid but doesn't provide low/medium/high runnable\nThere is one comment for all of low/medium/high runnable.","comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"50","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:50:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["112654","117941"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-112.94810807023342,37.28468360683833],[-112.94797886845578,37.28463947546015],[-112.94757860178976,37.28458020879356],[-112.94704160179054,37.28455600879363],[-112.94627746845845,37.28451907546031],[-112.94589026845904,37.28443760879378],[-112.94563886845941,37.28428787546068],[-112.94547386845966,37.284021408794445],[-112.9453920684598,37.28378100879479],[-112.9454206017931,37.28355520879518],[-112.9455120684596,37.28336700879544],[-112.9456190017928,37.28324980879563],[-112.94582940179248,37.283142008795835],[-112.9460064017922,37.28307320879594],[-112.94668406845778,37.282957608796096],[-112.94749306845654,37.28286740879622],[-112.9477288684562,37.28267667546322],[-112.94791120178922,37.2825472754634],[-112.9480384684557,37.28241880879693],[-112.94804960178902,37.28231427546376],[-112.94799920178906,37.28222727546387],[-112.94783686845604,37.28206507546412],[-112.94692740179073,37.281459208798424],[-112.94631480179169,37.28116707546553],[-112.94563660179273,37.280727808799554],[-112.9452376017934,37.28045407546665],[-112.94518826846013,37.280410875466714],[-112.94506600179363,37.280198675467034],[-112.94484146846067,37.27975740880106],[-112.94480460179403,37.27912620880204],[-112.94478526846075,37.27891220880235],[-112.94504806846032,37.27843540880309],[-112.94517926846015,37.27819147547019],[-112.94530540179329,37.27801360880375],[-112.94546680179303,37.277873608803986],[-112.94570560179267,37.27753447547116],[-112.94598706845886,37.277255208804945],[-112.94647380179146,37.276934008805426],[-112.94676426845768,37.276731475472445],[-112.94711580179046,37.2765004088061],[-112